  "body": "Spun off from the discussion in #12491. Test-case (note the `overflow: visible`):\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<style>\n  select {\n    box-sizing: border-box;\n    border: solid transparent 10px;\n    font-size: 40px;\n    width: 100px;\n    height: 100px;\n    padding: 30px;\n    outline: dashed 3px;\n    vertical-align: bottom;\n    overflow: visible;\n  }\n</style>\n\nAuto:\n\n<select style=\"appearance: auto\">\n  <option>XXX</option>\n</select><br>\n\nBase: <select style=\"appearance: base-select\">\n  <option>XXX</option>\n</select><br>\n\nBase + selectedcontent:\n\n<select style=\"appearance: base-select\">\n  <button>\n    <selectedcontent></selectedcontent>\n  </button>\n  <option>XXX</option>\n</select><br>\n```\n\nI would think the expected behavior, at least in base appearance mode, would be that the text overflows the `<select>`.\n\nIn Gecko, it only happens with the `Base + selectedcontent`, because the pseudo-element that we use to render the text has an internal clip.\n\nThis also relates to #12474.\n\ncc @bfgeek @josepharhar @annevk @keithamus ",
